  "term": "thought suppression",
  "definition": "Thought suppression is the deliberate effort to push away unwanted thoughts, especially ones that trigger negative feelings. Research described in the source links it with greater accessibility of the unwanted thought afterward, along with increased emotional and physical arousal, and with higher depression rates particularly under high stress.",
